From 358540b240bdf6e8465f7645637f212786cb5db6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jeff Heller <jeffrey_heller@yahoo.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:23:18 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] Android: don't abort when the deadlock protector is contended
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

QAndroidPlatformOpenGLWindow::eglSurface() calls qFatal() when it cannot
acquire the process-wide AndroidDeadlockProtector, killing the app. But
losing that race is not a deadlock: some unrelated subsystem — input
method, accessibility, permissions — is simply mid-call and holding the
single global flag.

The recoverable path is already written directly below the qFatal, just
unreachable, and the Vulkan backend in this same release does exactly
that (qandroidplatformvulkanwindow.cpp returns &m_vkSurface on the
identical condition). Both callers of eglSurface() already handle
EGL_NO_SURFACE: QAndroidPlatformOpenGLContext::makeCurrent() warns and
returns false, and QEGLPlatformContext::swapBuffers() has its own
"skip if using surfaceless context" guard. So the abort protects nothing
that the GL path cannot already survive.

Field data: since moving to Qt 6.11.1, every Android crash report the
app has received is this abort (2 of 2; 9 of 42 Android reports overall
since January). The window is the one a threaded render loop cannot
avoid — beginFrame/makeCurrent succeeds, the app state drops to
<= ApplicationHidden and destroySurface() clears m_androidSurfaceCreated
on the GUI thread, then endFrame/swapBuffers takes the surface-recreate
branch and dies on a contended flag.

No new log line: AndroidDeadlockProtector::acquire() already warns on
failure and names the current holder, which is strictly more useful than
anything this site could add.

Trade-offs, both strictly better than terminating:
- While a holder keeps the protector for a long stretch (a permission
  dialog), frames are dropped rather than rendered.
- A failed makeCurrent yields QRhi::FrameOpError, and qtdeclarative's
  threaded render loop re-posts an update only for FrameOpDeviceLost and
  FrameOpSwapChainOutOfDate, so nothing schedules a retry. Mid-session
  other events drive one; at startup there may briefly be none.

This is a local stop-gap. Upstream 735089 ("Android: drop deadlock
protector from EGL/Vk surface paths") removes the protector from these
paths entirely — which also removes the unsynchronised read of
AndroidDeadlockProtector::s_lockers that acquire() performs on failure,
now reachable once per frame rather than once per process lifetime.
It targets dev with no Pick-to: footer and sits seventh in a 17-change
series with no reviewer assigned. Drop this commit when that reaches the
Qt version we build against.

Task-number: QTBUG-140490
Task-number: QTBUG-144207
---
 .../android/qandroidplatformopenglwindow.cpp    | 17 ++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/plugins/platforms/android/qandroidplatformopenglwindow.cpp b/src/plugins/platforms/android/qandroidplatformopenglwindow.cpp
index c205727b..418a5fe1 100644
--- a/src/plugins/platforms/android/qandroidplatformopenglwindow.cpp
+++ b/src/plugins/platforms/android/qandroidplatformopenglwindow.cpp
@@ -65,7 +65,22 @@ EGLSurface QAndroidPlatformOpenGLWindow::eglSurface(EGLConfig config)
         static constexpr char funcName[] = "QAndroidPlatformOpenGLWindow::eglSurface()";
         QtAndroidPrivate::AndroidDeadlockProtector protector(funcName);
         if (!protector.acquire()) {
-            qFatal("Failed to acquire deadlock protector for %s.", funcName);
+            // Losing the race for the single process-wide protector is not a deadlock —
+            // another subsystem (input method, accessibility, permissions) is merely
+            // mid-call. Skip surface creation for this frame instead of terminating the
+            // process; the Vulkan backend in this same release already takes exactly this
+            // path (qandroidplatformvulkanwindow.cpp returns &m_vkSurface here), and both
+            // callers of eglSurface() handle EGL_NO_SURFACE — makeCurrent() warns and
+            // returns false, QEGLPlatformContext::swapBuffers() skips the swap. A later
+            // frame creates the surface once the protector is free.
+            // Debug, not warning, on purpose: acquire() itself already warns and names
+            // the current holder, so a second warning would only add noise to the log
+            // users attach to bug reports. This line stays as the string that proves a
+            // built plugin actually carries this patch (grep the .so for it).
+            // Upstream fix: https://codereview.qt-project.org/c/qt/qtbase/+/735089
+            // (QTBUG-140490, QTBUG-144207). Drop this once that reaches our Qt version.
+            qCDebug(lcQpaWindow, "[decenza-patch] deadlock protector contended in %s; "
+                                 "skipping surface creation for this frame.", funcName);
             return m_eglSurface;
         }
 
